## Communications
## Perovskites
Hole-Boosted $\mathsf{C u}(\mathsf{C r},\mathsf{M})\mathsf{O}_{2}$ Nanocrystals for All-Inorganic $\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}$ Perovskite Solar Cells
$\mathsf{C u}(\mathsf{C r},\mathsf{M})\mathsf{O}_{2}$ nanocrystals with hole boosting by increasing the amount of interstitial oxygen enables them to be promising HTMs for all-inorganic $\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}$ perovskite solar cells. The optimized device with $\mathsf{C u}(\mathsf{C r},\mathsf{B a})\mathsf{O}_{2}$ achieves a record efficiency as high as $10.79\%$ .
